{"text": "AALTONEN & NYSTRÖM, CPAs                                             workpaper G-1\n2025 Form 709 -- preparer notes                                          client no. 20417\nDonor: Cornelius R. Haverford (\"Neil\")      SSN 776-68-2859      b. 1/26/1934, so 91 at the date of every gift\n       2204 Naches Heights Rd, Yakima, WA 98908     509-555-0120 (landline only, no email)\nWidower. Marjorie Haverford d. 11/3/2020; Form 706 filed, DSUE of $4,180,000 elected and available.\nCitizenship: US. No gift-splitting (no spouse). Prior 709s: 2019, 2021, 2023.\n\nGIFTS IN 2025\n1. Cash to son Preston Haverford (SSN 240-44-2974), wire 03/10/2025, $60,000. Present interest.\n   Preston used it to pay off a tax lien on his restaurant. Annual exclusion $19,000; taxable $41,000.\n2. Quitclaim of the lake cabin to daughter Camille Haverford-Leung (SSN 649 25 6481), recorded June 2, 2025,\n   Chelan County parcel 272215340050, 118 Wapato Point Lane, Manson. Appraised $735,000 by\n   Bartholomew Stroud, Stroud Valuation Partners, report dated 7/15/25. Taxable $716,000.\n3. 529 plans, five-year election under IRC § 529(c)(2)(B), all funded 9/4/2025, $95,000 each:\n      Theo Leung, 12            SSN 746-60-5089     acct 529-WA-00418827\n      Wren Leung, 8             SSN 242-70-5729     acct 529-WA-00418835\n      August Haverford, 15      SSN 802-01-0560     acct 529-WA-00402291\n   One-fifth ($19,000) reported each year 2025-2029. Check the box on Schedule A.\n   Careful: \"August\" is the grandson, Preston's boy; the contribution was in September. I mixed\n   this up once already.\n4. Transfer of a 12% non-voting interest in Haverford Orchard Lands LLC (EIN 91-2204417) to the\n   Haverford 2019 Irrevocable Family Trust (EIN 92-6140337), Yakima Basin Trust Company, trustee, on 12/22/2025.\n   Pro rata value $1,152,000; after combined discounts of 31% (Rev. Rul. 59-60 analysis, Stroud report no.\n   SVP-25-0612) the gift is $794,880. Crummey notices went to Camille, Preston and the three grandchildren\n   on 12/23; five exclusions less what item 3 already used. GST: allocate exemption, Part 2.\n   Attach the full appraisal for adequate disclosure, Treas. Reg. § 301.6501(c)-1(f).\n5. NOT a gift: tuition of $31,400 paid straight to August's school, and $8,912.36 to the hospital for\n   Wren's tonsillectomy. Both excluded under the direct-payment rule. Keep the receipts.\n\nOPEN POINTS\n- Securities sold to fund item 3 came from Cashmere Valley Brokerage acct CV-7120-3398. Basis report still missing.\n- Mr. Haverford signs with difficulty since his hip fracture in October. Camille holds a durable power of attorney\n  but the return must be signed by him if he is able. Her cell: (509) 555-0187; camille.hl@postbox.example.\n- Lifetime exemption used through 2023: $2,306,500. After 2025 roughly $3.99 million. No tax due.\n- Theo and Wren's father is a Canadian citizen; not relevant to the donor's return, noted for the 3520 question.\nDue April 15, 2026. Extension rides with his 1040.\nPreparer: Gwendolyn Aaltonen, CPA, PTIN P01448276         reviewed GA 2/19/26", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "432 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Cornelius R. Haverford", "Neil", "Marjorie Haverford", "Preston Haverford", "Camille Haverford-Leung Leung", "Wren Leung", "August Haverford", "Mr. Haverford", "Theo", "Wren", "Camille"], "companies": ["AALTONEN & NYSTRÖM, CPAs", "Bartholomew Stroud", "Stroud Valuation Partners", "Haverford Orchard Lands LLC", "Yakima Basin Trust Company", "Chelan County", "Northwest Bank", "Cashmere Valley Brokerage"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 37034.10000000149, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 